NUM-42: keep a UH's own rain gage, and rescale a co-gage's rainfall for RDII

initGageData() re-pointed every unit hydrograph whose gage shares its rain
series with an earlier gage (its co-gage) to that earlier gage. Before 5.3.0
both gages gave the same rainfall, but since the per-gage rain scale factor
was added the UH gets the co-gage's scaling instead of its own. The UH now
keeps its gage; getRainfall() computes the co-gage's rainfall (once per RDII
step, as for any gage) and rescales it by the ratio of the two scale factors,
as gage_setState() does for subcatchments. With equal scale factors the
results are bit-identical to before.

Requires: NUM-41

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after NUM-41_swmm530.patch:
    git apply NUM-42_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c b/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c
index e86b171..b72e240 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c
@@ -1080,7 +1080,6 @@ void initGageData()
 //  Purpose: initializes state of Unit Hydrograph rain gages.
 //
 {
-    int i;                             // unit hyd. index
     int g;                             // rain gage index
 
     // --- first initialize the state of each rain gage
@@ -1092,21 +1091,6 @@ void initGageData()
         }
         gage_initState(g);
     }
-
-    // --- then flag each gage that is used by a Unit Hydrograph set
-    for (i=0; i<Nobjects[UNITHYD]; i++)
-    {
-        g = UnitHyd[i].rainGage;
-        if ( g >= 0 )
-        {
-            // --- if UH's gage uses same time series as a previous gage,
-            //     then assign the latter gage to the UH
-            if ( Gage[g].coGage >= 0 )
-            {
-                UnitHyd[i].rainGage = Gage[g].coGage;
-            }
-        }
-    }
 }
 
 //=============================================================================
@@ -1213,6 +1197,7 @@ void getRainfall(DateTime currentDate)
     int      j;                        // UH group index
     int      k;                        // UH index
     int      g;                        // rain gage index
+    int      cg;                       // index of gage's co-gage
     int      i;                        // past rainfall index
     int      month;                    // month of current date
     int      rainInterval;             // rainfall interval (sec)
@@ -1241,7 +1226,21 @@ void getRainfall(DateTime currentDate)
             Adjust.rainFactor = Adjust.rain[datetime_monthOfYear(gageDate)-1];
             if (!Gage[g].isCurrent)
             {
-                GageRain[g] = getGageRainfall(g, prevDate, currentDate);
+                // --- a gage sharing its rainfall record with an earlier
+                //     gage (its co-gage) uses the co-gage's rainfall,
+                //     rescaled by the ratio of their scale factors
+                cg = Gage[g].coGage;
+                if ( cg >= 0 )
+                {
+                    if (!Gage[cg].isCurrent)
+                    {
+                        GageRain[cg] = getGageRainfall(cg, prevDate, currentDate);
+                        Gage[cg].isCurrent = TRUE;
+                    }
+                    GageRain[g] = GageRain[cg] * Gage[g].scaleFactor /
+                                  Gage[cg].scaleFactor;
+                }
+                else GageRain[g] = getGageRainfall(g, prevDate, currentDate);
                 Gage[g].isCurrent = TRUE;
             }
 
